<<<
as equivalent to word or phrase; not more than potentially, because it so far smacks of pedantry that most people prefer to say word or phrase on the rare occasions when expression is not precise enough for the purpose, & l. gets left to the pedants.
===
as equivalent to *word or phrase*; not more than potentially, because it so far smacks of pedantry that most people prefer to say *word or phrase* on the rare occasions when *expression* is not precise enough for the purpose, & *l.* gets left to the pedants.
>>>

